  "category": "Matrix & Math",
  "description": "We define a magic square to be an n x n matrix of distinct positive integers from 1 to n^2 where the sum of any row, column, or diagonal of length n is always equal to the same number. Given a 3x3 matrix `s` with values in [1, 9], find the minimum cost to convert it into a magic square. (Cost = sum of |s[i][j] - magic[i][j]|).",
  "constraints": "s is a 3x3 matrix with integers in range [1, 9]\n\u2022 Time: O(1) | Space: O(1)",
  "function_name": "forming_magic_square",
